# Terraform working directory
.terraform/

# Terraform state files
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Crash logs
crash.log

# Terraform lock file (keep this if you want version pinning)
# .terraform.lock.hcl

# Local variable files
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Sensitive files
terraform-key.pem

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Professional practice:
- Keep .terraform.lock.hcl committed
- It locks provider versions
- Ensures reproducibility across machines

## Without .gitignore, you risk committing:
  - State file (contains resource IDs, sometimes sensitive info)
  - Private SSH key
  - Entire .terraform directory
  - Backend metadata
That’s how engineers accidentally expose infrastructure

# After creating .gitignore, run: git status
  - You should NOT see:
    - .terraform/
    - terraform.tfstate
    - terraform-key.pem
